                    </svg>
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Sub-Navigation for Safety Sections -->
    <nav class="subnav-bar" aria-label="Safety subsections">
        <div class="container subnav-container">
            <a href="#principles" class="subnav-link active">Safety Principles</a>
            <a href="#deployment" class="subnav-link">Deployment Safety</a>
            <a href="#security-privacy" class="subnav-link">Security &amp; Privacy</a>
            <a href="#transparency" class="subnav-link">Trust &amp; Transparency</a>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <main id="safety-tab-root">
        <!-- =============================================================
             1. TAB: SAFETY PRINCIPLES
             ============================================================= -->
        <div id="principles" class="tab-panel active">
            <!-- Hero -->
            <section class="safety-hero">
                <div class="container">
                    <span class="label-sm">SAFETY APPROACH &bull; Orains</span>
                    <h1 class="headline-xl">Engineering Intelligence Requires Engineering Discipline</h1>
                    <p class="body-lg">
                        At Orains, safety is not an additional layer added after development — it is part of how we design and evaluate ORAIN. Engineering systems operate where incorrect geometry, misunderstood requirements, invalid assumptions, or unreliable outputs can have consequences beyond the software itself.
                    </p>
                    <div style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                        <a href="#deployment" class="link-cta link-tab">Explore Deployment Validation Gates &rarr;</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Six Core Principles Grid -->
            <section class="section-block reveal">
                <div class="container">
                    <span class="label-sm">CORE FOUNDATIONS</span>
                    <h2 class="headline-md">Our Safety Principles</h2>
                    <p class="body-lg">
                        Our framework is built around validation, controlled execution, human oversight, and continuous evaluation across the entire engineering pipeline.
                    </p>

                    <div class="cards-grid-3">
                        <!-- Principle 01 -->
                        <div class="safety-card">
                            <div>
                                <span class="badge-mono">PRINCIPLE // 01</span>
                                <h3 class="headline-sm">Reason Before Construction</h3>
                                <p class="body-md">
                                    ORAIN is designed around separating engineering reasoning from geometry construction. Proposed designs are evaluated for intent, constraints, and physical feasibility before being translated into executable geometric operations.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-tag-footer">ERE REASONING KERNEL</div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Principle 02 -->
                        <div class="safety-card">
                            <div>
                                <span class="badge-mono">PRINCIPLE // 02</span>
                                <h3 class="headline-sm">Validate Before Delivery</h3>
                                <p class="body-md">
                                    Generated geometry is never treated as correct simply because it can be rendered. Geometry requires structural, topological, and computational validation before it is considered suitable for downstream engineering use.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-tag-footer">TOPOLOGICAL VALIDATION</div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Principle 03 -->
                        <div class="safety-card">
                            <div>
                                <span class="badge-mono">PRINCIPLE // 03</span>
                                <h3 class="headline-sm">Human Oversight</h3>
                                <p class="body-md">
                                    ORAIN is designed to assist engineers, not remove engineering accountability. Critical engineering decisions, parameter sign-offs, and final tolerances remain subject to qualified human review.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-tag-footer">HUMAN-IN-THE-LOOP</div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Principle 04 -->
                        <div class="safety-card">
                            <div>
                                <span class="badge-mono">PRINCIPLE // 04</span>
                                <h3 class="headline-sm">Controlled Execution</h3>
                                <p class="body-md">
                                    Intelligent systems should not have unrestricted authority over engineering software or infrastructure. Execution environments are isolated, controlled, and permissioned according to least-privilege principles.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-tag-footer">SANDBOXED BOUNDARIES</div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Principle 05 -->
                        <div class="safety-card">
                            <div>
                                <span class="badge-mono">PRINCIPLE // 05</span>
                                <h3 class="headline-sm">Traceable Decisions</h3>
                                <p class="body-md">
                                    Where possible, engineering transformations maintain structured feature graphs and dependency representations that allow engineers to inspect exactly how an output was produced.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-tag-footer">PARAMETRIC AUDIT TRAIL</div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Principle 06 -->
                        <div class="safety-card">
                            <div>
                                <span class="badge-mono">PRINCIPLE // 06</span>
                                <h3 class="headline-sm">Continuous Evaluation</h3>
                                <p class="body-md">
                                    Safety is an ongoing process. Reasoning models, geometry kernels, constraint solvers, and deployment environments are continuously benchmarked as the platform evolves.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-tag-footer">EMPIRICAL BENCHMARKING</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>
        </div>

        <!-- =============================================================
             2. TAB: DEPLOYMENT SAFETY & VALIDATION GATES
             ============================================================= -->
        <div id="deployment" class="tab-panel">
            <section class="section-block reveal">
                <div class="container">
                    <span class="label-sm">GOVERNANCE &amp; CONTROL</span>
                    <h2 class="headline-md">Deploying Engineering Intelligence Responsibly</h2>
                    <p class="body-lg">
                        Deploying an AI system into an engineering workflow requires more than model performance. The surrounding environment, permissions, validation mechanisms, and human oversight all matter.
                    </p>

                    <!-- Deployment Pipeline Strip -->
                    <div style="margin-top: 3.5rem;">
                        <span class="label-sm">A RESPONSIBLE DEPLOYMENT PRINCIPLE</span>
                        <div class="pipeline-strip" style="margin-top: 0.8rem;">
                            <div class="pipeline-step"><span>01</span> Use Case</div>
                            <span class="pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</span>
                            <div class="pipeline-step"><span>02</span> Risk</div>
                            <span class="pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</span>
                            <div class="pipeline-step"><span>03</span> Permissions</div>
                            <span class="pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</span>
                            <div class="pipeline-step"><span>04</span> Validation</div>
                            <span class="pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</span>
                            <div class="pipeline-step"><span>05</span> Human Oversight</div>
                            <span class="pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</span>
                            <div class="pipeline-step"><span>06</span> Monitoring</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="cards-grid-2" style="margin-top: 4rem;">
                        <!-- Left Card: Validation Gates -->
                        <div class="safety-card">
                            <div>
                                <span class="badge-mono">GATEWAY CRITERIA</span>
                                <h3 class="headline-sm">Algorithmic Validation Gates</h3>
                                <p class="body-md">
                                    Generated geometry and CAD operations pass through strict multi-stage validation gates before being released to downstream simulation, meshing, or manufacturing pipelines:
                                </p>
                                <ul class="spec-list">
                                    <li>Geometric validity &amp; boundary evaluation</li>
                                    <li>Topological consistency &amp; manifold integrity</li>
                                    <li>Constraint verification &amp; dimensional bounds</li>
                                    <li>Operation execution validation</li>
                                    <li>Self-intersection &amp; collision detection</li>
